---

## 📖 Overview

**SwarmMind** is a full-stack AI platform that brings the collective intelligence of nature into real-world problem solving. Inspired by how ants find the shortest path to food using pheromone trails and how bees coordinate hive decisions, SwarmMind deploys **hundreds to thousands of lightweight autonomous agents** that cooperate in a distributed manner to solve large-scale optimization problems.

The system implements **Ant Colony Optimization (ACO)**, a bio-inspired metaheuristic algorithm, to tackle NP-hard problems such as:
- 🗺️ **Travelling Salesman Problem (TSP)** — Shortest route through N cities
- 📅 **Job Scheduling** — Optimal task-to-machine assignment
- 🚚 **Logistics Routing** — Fleet delivery optimization
- 🚨 **Disaster Response** — Relief resource allocation

Built with a **Python (FastAPI) backend** and a **React-based interactive frontend**, the platform provides real-time swarm visualization, live pheromone heatmaps, convergence analytics, and AI-generated explanations powered by **Google Gemini**. Runs efficiently on **CPU-only** environments — no GPU required.

---

## ✨ Key Features

### 🐜 Swarm Simulation Engine
- Configurable number of agents (10 to 5000+)
- Real-time pheromone evolution
- Tunable parameters: α (alpha), β (beta), evaporation rate, Q
- Iteration-by-iteration convergence tracking

### 🎯 Multi-Problem Support
| Problem Type | Description |
|--------------|-------------|
| **TSP** | Find shortest route visiting all cities exactly once |
| **Scheduling** | Assign jobs to machines for minimum makespan |
| **Logistics** | Optimize multi-vehicle delivery routes |
| **Disaster Response** | Allocate limited relief to maximum-impact zones |

### 📊 Live Visualization
- Canvas-based ant animation (every agent visible in motion)
- Pheromone heatmap (edge intensity → color)
- Best-path highlight in glowing neon
- Convergence chart (best distance vs iterations)

### 🤖 AI-Powered Insights
- Google Gemini generates natural-language explanations:
  - Why this path is optimal
  - How the swarm converged
  - Real-world implications

### 🎨 Modern UI/UX
- Dark theme with neon accents (cyan, purple, orange)
- Glassmorphism cards, smooth Framer Motion animations
- Fully responsive design

### ⚡ CPU-Optimized
- No GPU required — runs on any laptop
- NumPy vectorization for fast matrix operations
- Async task execution for non-blocking simulations

